tags: pci-function-id, pci-id

The identity of the model of a PCI device: two 16-bit numbers in the configuration
space of a PCI function, which the maker of the device sets. A PCI Express device has
the same two numbers at the same places.

=== formal
class=concept
device=the 16-bit number at bytes 2 and 3 of the configuration space of the function, little-endian
name=pci-function-id
text=<vendor>:<device>, each as 4 digits of base 16, with the letters a to f in lowercase
vendor=the 16-bit number at bytes 0 and 1 of the configuration space of the function, little-endian
